course: dictionary
lesson: 15630
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «The Templar knights guarded the roads to Jerusalem for travelling Christians.» Knights, roads and guarding point to the history of the Crusades, so a Templar is a knight.
explain: «The Templar lawyer checked the papers in her office near the law courts.» Here lawyer, office and courts point to law, so Templar means a lawyer who works in the Temple, an area of London law courts and offices. Always ask: what does the rest of the sentence tell me? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Capital letters and phrases help too. The Knights Templar is a name for a group of knights from history. If you are not sure, read on for more clues, or check a dictionary, which will settle it.
fact: A Templar can be a Knight Templar: a member of a religious order of knights.
fact: The Knights Templar were founded about 1119 to protect Christian pilgrims travelling to Jerusalem.
fact: The Templars were famous fighting monks in the Crusades, and they were shut down in 1312.
fact: In law, a Templar is a lawyer who works in the Temple, an area of law courts and offices in London.
fact: Many legends and myths about Templar treasure are made up, so be careful what you believe.
exercise: «The Templars guarded the roads to Jerusalem for Christian pilgrims.» What is a Templar in this sentence? | *A knight who belonged to a religious order | A shopkeeper who sold bread | A lawyer in a London office | A king who ruled Jerusalem
exercise: Mia visited an old «Templar church» in the village. What does Templar tell us here? | It means a very tall church | It is a kind of boat | It means a church only for lawyers | *It is linked to the Knights Templar
exercise: «The Templar lawyer checked the contract at the court.» What does Templar mean here? | A pilgrim walking to Jerusalem | A monk who fought in battles | *A lawyer who works in the Temple in London | A type of old coin
test: In what year were the Templars shut down? | *1312 | 1119 | 1066 | 1453
test: Are the stories about Templar treasure true? | Yes, every one has been proven | Yes, the Templars buried gold in London | *No, many of them are made up | Only the ones found in books
exam: Which sentence uses templar in the legal sense? | «The Templar church was very old.» | «The Templar knights rode to Jerusalem.» | *«The Templar lawyer checked the papers at the court in London.» | «Templars fought in the Crusades.»
